## 1. Project name and goal

enggenie is a role-based SDLC skill suite (pure Markdown SKILL.md files plus subagent prompt templates, no runtime, no build, no npm dependency) for AI coding assistants: Claude Code, Cursor, GitHub Copilot CLI, Gemini CLI, OpenCode. It encodes the SDLC context a senior team carries implicitly: spec (pm-refine), design/plan (dev-brainstorm, dev-plan), TDD build (dev-implement, dev-tdd, dev-debug, dev-commit), review (review-code with 3 parallel lenses, review-design), QA (qa-verify, qa-test), ship (deploy-ship), memory (memory-recall, needs claude-mem), plus a gateway skill (enggenie). Author: Badru Siddique (Engineering Manager at Hudl; this is a personal open-source project, MIT). The session covered Jun 1 - Jun 22 2026: v2.7.0 and v3.0.0 releases, v3.1.0 / v3.1.1 changes (committed locally, NOT tagged, NOT pushed), a SessionStart hook (committed, NOT pushed), docs/marketing work (Medium follow-up post draft, LinkedIn draft, README overhaul, SEO repo metadata).

