## 6. Decisions already made - do not revisit (details in DECISIONS.md)

- No "Architect" role. Brainstorm/plan are Dev activities: dev-brainstorm, dev-plan. 6 roles: PM, Dev, Reviewer, QA, Deploy, Memory.
- Estimation default is T-shirt sizing by relative complexity, never hours; XL means decompose.
- UX/design artifacts are INPUTS to pm-refine (design happens upstream); absent design => spec PROVISIONAL; review-design is an exit checkpoint when a design exists.
- Any change that adds capability = major version (user rejected a 2.8.0 plan; v3.0.0 shipped with docs overhaul). Documentation must sell: before/after, real terminal output, diagrams.
- Multi-lens review: 3 anonymous lenses (security, engineering, test) + consolidation agent keeping the name code-reviewer-agent.md; severity words exactly Blocking / Advisory / Observation.
- Plagiarism rules re developer.ai: concepts only; no named personas (Alice, Bob, Jekyll, Hyde etc.), no "Prime Directive" phrase, no HTML comment tagging, no verbatim spec text. Same caution for gstack and for the user's own earlier Medium post (no verbatim reuse).
- Project-first configuration: detect and defer to project conventions (commit rules, existing review agents, mobile vs web) and tell the user which source is used; never blend two convention systems.
- Pre-release QA gate (6 categories, parallel subagents) before every commit/release (user standing requirement).
- Commit style: small batches, human-like messages, no AI co-author tags (user memory feedback_commit_style). NOTE: the session-level attribution reminder said to add a Co-Authored-By line; the user's rule takes precedence.
- Never push to main without the user's explicit "yes" (Claude Code auto-mode classifier denied unauthorized pushes twice).
- Hyphens only (no em-dashes) in all content.

