## 8. Constraints and patterns to follow

- Three locations per skill: skills/<name>/SKILL.md (canonical, tracked), .agents/skills/<name>/ (real dirs, gitignored mirror), .claude/skills/<name> (symlinks to ../../.agents/skills/<name>, gitignored). After editing skills/, `cp` into .agents/skills/ (skills-lock.json is also gitignored). The mirror is NOT currently in sync (dev-tdd, qa-test/scripts/with_server.py differ; dev-commit and using-enggenie missing) - see section 9.
- Rename/refactor sweep pattern: sed -i '' across skills, docs, README, CLAUDE.md, plans; leave CHANGELOG history untouched and add a new entry.
- Verification before any commit (CLAUDE.md in repo + user memory): functionality, persona walkthrough, skills-expert handoff chains, security, marketplace/platform docs, zero-mentions scan (superpowers / Hudl / personal paths). Also: no em-dashes, no architect-design / architect-plan refs, 4 agent files in review-code/agents, skills/ vs .agents/ diff clean.
- Subagent templates use placeholder tokens like {GIT_DIFF}; lens agents must stay in their own domain; round 2+ lenses surface only new or worsened findings.
- Skills announce themselves ("I'm using enggenie:<skill> ..."), include a model recommendation, wait for user approval on commits/specs, never auto-invoke the next skill.
- Docs tone: relatable, concrete, real terminal output from the "heist" demo app (Next.js + TypeScript + Firebase/Firestore), no jargon-first openings.
- Medium/LinkedIn writing: first person, casual, section-heading emojis, short sentences, [GIF:]/[SCREENSHOT:]/[IMAGE:] placeholders clearly marked; LinkedIn is short, hook-first, ends with a question.
- Do NOT modify ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md or user config without explicit user approval (classifier blocked it once; user later approved and it was edited).
- Read-only default on the repo until the user asks to commit/push.

